<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">How to Download Twitch Clips</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Twitch clips capture the best moments from live streams. Whether you want to save your own highlights or a clip from a streamer who allows downloads, this guide explains how to do it easily.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">What are Twitch clips?</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Clips are short segments of a Twitch stream, usually 5 to 60 seconds long. They are created by viewers or streamers and shared on Twitch and social media. Clips are public unless the channel restricts them.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">How to download a Twitch clip</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Open the Twitch clip in your browser.</li>
        <li>Copy the URL from the address bar. It looks like <code>https://clips.twitch.tv/ClipName</code>.</li>
        <li>Go to <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %></a>.</li>
        <li>Paste the URL and click <strong>Get Video</strong>.</li>
        <li>Choose MP4 and download the clip.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Downloading your own clips</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Streamers can download their own clips directly from the Twitch Creator Dashboard. However, using a downloader can be faster if you only have a clip link and need an MP4.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Respect streamer rights</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Twitch content is owned by the streamer. Save clips for personal use only unless the streamer has given permission. Do not monetize or redistribute clips without authorization.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Can I download full Twitch VODs?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Full past broadcasts may be downloadable if they are public and the streamer allows it. Some VODs are subscriber-only.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Do Twitch clips have watermarks?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">No, downloaded Twitch clips usually do not have a Twitch watermark, but the streamer's branding may appear in the video.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Why is my clip not loading?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Check that the clip is still public and has not been deleted by the streamer or Twitch.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
